' Design pattern — Database per Service.
'
' Two services rather than all six: the rule is what matters, not the
' inventory, and six service/database pairs lay out ~3:1 and shrink to a strip.
'
' ONE forbidden arrow, not two. The earlier version drew both directions; the
' two dashed edges crossed between the databases and their two «ممنوع» labels
' landed on top of the two «تقرأ وتكتب» labels, so the middle of the figure was
' a knot. One arrow states the same rule and leaves the figure readable.
'
' The legitimate cross-service path is drawn too — otherwise the figure says
' what is forbidden without saying what replaces it. The full list of the five
' databases is prose now, not a note box.
@startuml
!include _style.puml
!include _pattern-style.puml

rectangle "خدمة إدارة المستخدمين" as UMS
rectangle "خدمة الفصول الدراسية" as CS

database "users_db" as UDB
database "classroomdb" as CDB

' Pin each service directly above its own database. Without this, smetana
' orders the two rows independently and the ownership arrows themselves cross.
UMS -[hidden]right- CS
UDB -[hidden]right- CDB

UMS --> UDB : تملك
CS --> CDB : تملك

CS -[dashed]-> UDB : <b>ممنوع</b>
' Short label on purpose: the two services sit side by side, so whatever this
' edge is labelled sets the width of the whole figure. Spelling out "نداء
' داخلي أو حدث على الناقل" here took it to 2.64:1, past the README's 2.2.
CS -left-> UMS : عبر الناقل
@enduml
